# The binary is a statically linked musl artifact on purpose: one package must
# install unchanged on every supported release, which a libc6-linked binary
# cannot do, and there is no Debian-packaged musl runtime to depend on instead.
#
# Two lines, not one, because lintian sees a different shape per architecture
# and fires a different tag. On amd64 a musl release build is static-PIE --
# ET_DYN with a PT_DYNAMIC and no NEEDED entries -- and
# lintian's Binaries::Static skips its tag for anything whose file type reads
# as a shared object or pie executable, so Binaries::Prerequisites reports a
# shared library missing its dependencies instead. On arm64 the same build is a
# plain ET_EXEC and the expected tag fires.
#
# Measured on lintian 2.116.3 and 2.122.0, identically.
# Re-check either half with `file` on the built binary and
# `lintian --show-overrides <deb>`: the tag that fires on this architecture
# shows as an `O:` line, and the other one is simply not evaluated.
kerbridge-issuerd [amd64]: shared-library-lacks-prerequisites [usr/sbin/issuerd]
kerbridge-issuerd [arm64]: statically-linked-binary [usr/sbin/issuerd]

# kbsetup is the second binary in this package and takes the same pair.
kerbridge-issuerd [amd64]: shared-library-lacks-prerequisites [usr/sbin/kbsetup]
kerbridge-issuerd [arm64]: statically-linked-binary [usr/sbin/kbsetup]

# The postinst names /usr/sbin/kbsetup absolutely to print what is still
# outstanding, for the same reason kerbridge-config's `config` script names
# /usr/bin/kbconfig -- this package installs that binary at that path, so it
# cannot move without this package moving it, and a maintainer script that
# resolved its own binary through PATH would run as root against whatever
# answered first. That override carries the full reasoning.
#
# No context on the line, deliberately: with one the override names a line
# number, and the first edit above it turns this into an unused override that a
# gate set to --fail-on error,warning would then trip over.
kerbridge-issuerd: command-with-path-in-maintainer-script
